+# Tasks
+
+## 1. Persistence layer
+
+- [x] 1.1 Add `CouponRedemptionRepository` (`src/repositories/couponRedemptionRepository.ts`) exposing `insert(orderId, couponCode, discountCents, createdAt)` and a `transaction(fn)` helper that wraps work on the shared connection in `BEGIN IMMEDIATE` / `COMMIT` / `ROLLBACK`; verify with a repository test that a redemption row is written and rolled back on throw
+- [x] 1.2 Add `OrderRepository.applyCoupon(id, discountCents, finalAmountCents, couponCode)` and `CouponRepository.incrementUsedCount(code)`; verify each with repository tests asserting the updated row
+
+## 2. Service rules
+
+- [x] 2.1 Give `OrderService` a `CouponRepository` and `CouponRedemptionRepository` and implement `applyCoupon(id, couponCode)` performing fail-fast validation (exists, `ACTIVE`, within validity window via the injected clock, order `PENDING` and coupon-free, `amountCents >= minAmountCents`, usage limit) and integer discount math with cap and non-negative clamp; verify with service-level tests for each `AppError` code and amount
+- [x] 2.2 Make the successful application atomic (order update + `used_count` increment + redemption insert inside `transaction`) and persist `couponCode`/`discountCents`/`finalAmountCents`; verify a successful call updates the order and increments `usedCount`
+- [x] 2.3 Wire the new repositories into `createApp` in `src/app.ts`; verify `npm run build` type-checks
+
+## 3. HTTP route
+
+- [x] 3.1 Register `POST /orders/:id/apply-coupon` in `src/routes/orders.ts` parsing `:id` with `parseId` and the body's `couponCode`, returning 200 with the updated order; verify with an in-process `app.request` test
+
+## 4. Integration verification
+
+- [x] 4.1 Add end-to-end tests covering the acceptance criteria — valid coupon returns 200, unknown/disabled/expired/below-minimum coupons return 400, expiry uses the injected clock; verify `npm test` passes
+- [x] 4.2 Run `npm run build` and `npm test` together and confirm both succeed
